      "content": "While executive privilege is constitutionally rooted to protect candid legal advice and national security, its unchecked expansion recentralizes legislative oversight power and weakens congressional ability to investigate imminent threats to democracy. The stronger legal position argues that privilege should remain narrow and custodial rather than an expansive shield, ensuring the separation of powers prevents the presidency from evading accountability. Ultimately, preserving checks and balances requires the judiciary to mandate disclosure whenever diplomatic, national, or security confidentiality is jeopardized.",
